docs
# The client is a static bundle and a Capacitor shell — no part of the server
# image needs its source. Its *manifest* is a different matter: `npm ci` against
# a workspace lockfile refuses to run unless every workspace named in
# package-lock.json has its package.json present, so excluding this one file
# broke the build with "/packages/client/package.json: not found".
#
# That went unnoticed because the `image` job only runs once `check` passes, and
# `check` was red for days. A conditional job cannot report a bug it never runs.
packages/client
!packages/client/package.json
*.log

# The same two patterns `.gitignore` carries, and for a sharper reason.
#
# `.gitignore` does not govern a build context: an FCM private key sitting
# untracked in a working tree would be copied into an image layer and stay there
# forever, in something that gets pushed to a registry. Firebase downloads these
# as `<project>-firebase-adminsdk-<hash>-<digits>.json`, which is why there are
# two patterns rather than one.
*service-account*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
